  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2017-10-24T05:13:49.477Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If someone is playing music, and I dance to it, from everyone else's perspective, I'm about a beat behind (depending on their ping, and my ping, and the audio source). Sometimes I try to perform moves about 75ms ahead of the beat to compensate, but it's really difficult. It'd be nice if audio and movement data could be buffered so they could be replayed together in-sync. I dunno how it'd work in practice with more than one person, though, or in situations where the dancer isn't also the audio source. Maybe the answer lies in tons of tiny netcode optimizations, instead of a direct solution.",
